-- SHADOW-SEMANTICS S2-DECL (d), (e): `hub` re-exports `IA.mth : a -> Int` (impl
-- `Int`) and `IB.mth : f a -> Int` (impl `List`).  Inference types each occurrence
-- against the first `mth` in scope, here `IA`'s, so at `mth 3` the declared
-- `f a -> Int` of `IB` does not instantiate to `Int -> Int`.  That mismatch says
-- which declaration came first, not which one is meant, so `IB` has no answer, the
-- set is undecided, and `mth 3` is the located `T-AMBIGUOUS-METHOD`.  Never
-- `(100, 4)`, which this order printed while a mismatch selected nothing and the
-- swapped order (`swapped.mdk`) rejected.
import hub.{IA, IB, mth}

main = println (mth [1, 2], mth 3)
